WEBVTT

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:04.490
A detection design should explain what behavior is being detected, why it matters,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.400
what data sources are required, what logic is used, and what assumptions exist.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.800
The design should also describe expected false positives, severity, enrichment, ownership,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.320
and what analysts should do when the detection fires.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.575
Good documentation helps future analysts and engineers understand the detection without

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:20.320
guessing.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.305
It also supports review, tuning, handoff, and accountability.

00:00:23.305 --> 00:00:26.680
Detections that cannot be explained are difficult to trust, tune, or maintain.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.380
A clear design makes the detection easier to operate as a long-lived asset.
